WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.600
Here we go.

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.735
Newspapers across

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.302
the country

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.703
are dropping the Dilbert

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.505
comic strip after its creator,

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:05.839
Scott

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:08.408
Adams, went on a stunning racist

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.776
tirade this weekend, calling

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.643
black Americans

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.611
a hate group

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.113
and advising white people

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.948
to stay away from them.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.416
And as Polo Sandoval

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.518
has the story this morning for us, Polo,

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.285
good morning to you.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.086
What's up? With this?

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.221
Yeah, guys, good morning to you.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.188
So basically,

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.090
he is doubling down on the comments

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.892
that he made earlier this week saying

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:26.926
that they were completely

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.028
taken out of context.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.863
The newspapers know that ran

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.296
his strip

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.664
for decades,

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.665
are now severing ties

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:32.999
with him,

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.134
saying that his comments

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:36.836
were part of a racist tirade

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:38.538
Yes.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:38.838
You know,

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.307
nearly half of all blacks

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.443
are not okay with white people.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.577
That's a hate group.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.246
That was a comment that may have ended.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.515
Scott Adams his newspaper career,

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:49.382
the Dilbert creator,

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.417
referencing a poll

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.484
from the conservative firm

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.687
Rasmussen Reports that indicated 53%

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.955
of black Americans agree

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:58.224
with the statement it's okay to be white

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.427
leading the other 47%

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.562
to say they disagree or aren't sure.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:03.930
The Anti-Defamation

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.664
League has noted

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.866
that that phrase has a long history

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.868
in the white supremacist movement.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:09.803
The best advice

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.970
I would give to white

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.872
people is to get the hell away

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.040
from black people.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.475
He continued to double down

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.409
throughout his show,

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.111
The Washington Post, Los Angeles

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.345
Times and USA Today,

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.114
among the hundreds of newspapers

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.115
that denounced Adams

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.817
and quickly pulled Dilbert.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:26.352
USA Today newspaper CEO Mike Read.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.289
It was, frankly, an easy decision.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.091
We found the remarks

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.659
hateful, hurtful,

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:34.561
and then just crossed the line.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.029
But not everyone agrees.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:39.032
Twitter CEO Elon Musk coming to Adams's

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.668
defense, tweeting, The media is racist.

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.369
Adams has since tweeted

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.205
that he was only advising people

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.973
to avoid hate and suggested

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:47.907
that the cancelation

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:48.708
of his cartoon

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.743
signals that free speech in America

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.911
is under assault.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.347
We believe in free speech.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:57.083
We believe in creating

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.753
a place for differing points of view.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.689
But there's a line

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.157
that gets crossed where

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:08.061
things become racism.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:11.197
And and that's not an area

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.265
we choose to

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:15.602
to traffic in or participate in.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.603
But he rejected a company

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:17.303
that was responsible

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.805
for distributing that comic strip.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.073
Still waiting to hear back, guys.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:20.573
But have to tell you,

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.175
after watching hours

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.676
and hours of his latest

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:24.511
streams,

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.278
it's really hard

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.680
to gauge exactly how worried he is.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.716
I'll tell you why he loves attention.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:30.583
It's not me saying it.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.018
He actually said it over the weekend

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.319
on one of his streams.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.487
And he also recognized

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.722
that he was completely aware

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:36.923
that this was basically going

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.858
to open up the floodgates.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.293
And when he made these

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.294
bombshell remarks,

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:44.197
so he is getting a bit of what he wanted.

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.365
But the question will it be

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.866
more than what he bargained for,

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.401
especially since he says that he expects

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.569
to lose a majority of the income

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.703
in the coming days? Right.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.738
There are many times

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.940
when people are taken out of context

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.575
or they need explaining or whatever.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:56.910
But his comments were

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.912
that's not what's with these comments.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:02:59.646
He keeps saying

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.547
that's not what I meant to say,

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:02.415
but it is exactly what he calls

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:03.950
it, useful provocation.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:04.450
He wanted to

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.852
start a conversation in guys.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.986
But there are many ways

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:07.921
to start a conversation

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.322
about race in America

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.791
that doesn't include calling

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.494
black Americans what he called them.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:15.862
So I think that this will be

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.096
certainly one to watch.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:17.730
And as you continue

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.098
to hear major newspapers,

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:19.966
not just here in the U.S.,

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.068
but around the world, dropping the Strip.

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.436
What will he do next?

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.470
Yeah, and it's important to note

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.005
that the poll that started

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.707
all of this that he was talking about,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.375
they are not talking about their data.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.677
There are people have cast doubt on

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:32.712
how accurate it is

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:33.446
and what it looks like.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.515
And if people are trying to vote on it,

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:36.783
to change the outcome of it.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.850
So I think that's an also

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.785
an important context

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.053
of what he's even talking about

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:40.954
in the first place. Really?

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.222
Does he say he's being canceled?

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:43.122
Is that what he thinks?

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.457
That's what he says.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.225
I wonder

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.926
if he's perhaps seeing himself

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.995
as sort of this free speech martyr.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.029
Again, we'll have to see

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.097
as more of these newspapers

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:51.698
drop his work

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.600
after decades and for 30 years,

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.568
his speech comes with consequences.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.370
Yeah. Thank you for that.

